KG42.register("rules-f10cb1ac1490cba46e0fd1e4",{"id":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R010","paper":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"The local clearing price is established when only one qualified bidder remains and equals the submitted price of the last second qualified bidder, as in the stated Vickrey auction model. Scope: Hour-ahead reverse auction in the grid-connected microgrid; general pricing description. Condition: Only one qualified bidder remains in the auction. Establishment of the local clearing price is conditional on the total offered power submission meeting demand in the stated example. Scope: Worked example described as the 17th h of the microgrid reverse auction. Condition: The total submitted power meets demand in this worked example. When two generation units qualify simultaneously in the stated example, the local clearing price is the value of the last bid. Scope: Worked example described as the 17th h of the microgrid reverse auction. Condition: Two generation units qualify at the same time in this worked example.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply","matching.counterparties","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"bidding.supply","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e021"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E002","source":"pricing.local","target":"matching.counterparties","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e021"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Hour-ahead reverse auction in the grid-connected microgrid; general pricing description. | Worked example described as the 17th h of the microgrid reverse auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e021"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The local clearing price is established when only one qualified bidder remains and equals the submitted price of the last second qualified bidder, as in the stated Vickrey auction model. Scope: Hour-ahead reverse auction in the grid-connected microgrid; general pricing description. Condition: Only one qualified bidder remains in the auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e012"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Establishment of the local clearing price is conditional on the total offered power submission meeting demand in the stated example. Scope: Worked example described as the 17th h of the microgrid reverse auction. Condition: The total submitted power meets demand in this worked example.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e021"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C003","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"When two generation units qualify simultaneously in the stated example, the local clearing price is the value of the last bid. Scope: Worked example described as the 17th h of the microgrid reverse auction. Condition: Two generation units qualify at the same time in this worked example.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e021"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. Hardware setup and agent platform. continues until only one qualiﬁed bidder remains in the a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The process continues until only one qualified bidder remains in the auction. Accordingly, the market clearing price is established, which is the submitted price of the last second qualified bidder as in the Vickrey auction model."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e021","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"VI. Results and Discussions","anchor_text":"ed amount of power is higher than the demand, the aggregator ed agent runs another round by lowering","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":"Table II","image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"According to Table II, the amounts of power that can be bid on inverter1 and inverter2 during the 17th h are 500 and 100 kW, respectively. Since the total submission meets the demand, the auction process ends and the market clearing price is established. Since two generation units qualify at the same time, the market clearing price is the value of the last bid."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational decision variable is explicitly defined in the supplied pricing-rule evidence. The source names 'market clearing price', 'last bid', and 'last second qualified bidder', but supplies no formal variable symbol, domain, or decision role. The 600 kW demand and 500/100 kW bid amounts are worked-example quantities, not declared decision variables; adding variables for them here would invent source meanings.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter with a source-defined symbol, domain, and role is declared in the rule evidence. The example's 600 kW demand and 500/100 kW bid amounts are data for the 17th-hour illustration, and the clearing-price relation is not given as a parameterized formula. The current frozen graph contains functional nodes rather than typed quantity objects, so no theta object is asserted."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e012","quote":"The process continues until only one qualified bidder remains in the auction. Accordingly, the market clearing price is established, which is the submitted price of the last second qualified bidder as in the Vickrey auction model."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e021","quote":"Since the total submission meets the demand, the auction process ends and the market clearing price is established."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e021","quote":"Since two generation units qualify at the same time, the market clearing price is the value of the last bid."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"1fcd33703dc5584aa77a8e1f2a177fce7a5f56c852288ee725c24423e914c830","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The frozen rule contains a verbal Vickrey-style local-clearing-price rule, but the supplied B quotations do not define a formal symbol, domain, unit-bearing variable, parameter or quantifier for the market-clearing price, the submitted price of the 'last second qualified bidder', or the 'last bid'. The 17th-hour example gives concrete quantities (600 kW demand and 500/100 kW bids), but the rule text does not state a general formula linking them to the clearing price. The evidence also contains unresolved conflicts: e012 says the process continues until only one qualified bidder remains yet sets the price at the submitted price of the last second qualified bidder, while e021 says two generation units qualify simultaneously and the price is the value of the last bid. The frozen graph has functional nodes and conditional edges but no quantity objects for these referents, so no faithful expression can be emitted without C.1 revision. Existing phi entries are retained as not_formalized. B evidence remains unreviewed; no claim of verified source correctness or independent review is made.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","matching.counterparties"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E002"],"rationale":"C001 is member-constrained to pricing.local and matching.counterparties. Frozen edge E002 records that pricing.local is conditional_on matching.counterparties for C001/C003. This binding records the graph relationship only; no formula is asserted."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","node_ids":["pricing.local","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"C002 is member-constrained to pricing.local and bidding.supply. Frozen edge E001 records that pricing.local is conditional_on bidding.supply for C002. This binding records the graph relationship only; the example's numeric quantities are not promoted to formal parameters."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C003","node_ids":["pricing.local","matching.counterparties"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E002"],"rationale":"C003 is member-constrained to pricing.local and matching.counterparties. Frozen edge E002 records that pricing.local is conditional_on matching.counterparties for C001/C003. This binding records the graph relationship only; the undefined 'last bid' is not represented by an invented symbol."}],"revision_requests":["C.1: add or authorize source-grounded quantity objects for the market clearing price (unit $/kWh) and for the submitted price of the relevant qualified bidder, with evidence v141-b-g02-e012 and v141-b-g02-e021, and bind them to pricing.local. State whether these are operational outputs or parameters rather than inventing a variable role.","C.1: define the ordered qualified-bidder referent for 'last second qualified bidder' in v141-b-g02-e012. Determine whether it means the second-to-last qualifying bidder, the last losing bid, or another rule, and add an ordered set/index only if source-supported; otherwise record the referent as unresolved.","C.1: resolve or explicitly preserve the branch conflict between v141-b-g02-e012 ('only one qualified bidder remains' but price equals the last second qualified bidder's submitted price) and v141-b-g02-e021 ('two generation units qualify at the same time' and price equals the value of the last bid). Provide source-supported conditions for one remaining bidder versus two simultaneous qualifiers, or keep both as unresolved alternatives.","C.1: for C002, define formal referents for 'total submitted power' and 'demand' and the meaning of 'meets demand' (equality versus sufficiency). If the 17th-hour values (600 kW demand; 500 kW inverter1 bid; 100 kW inverter2 bid) are to be used, label them explicitly as example parameters with units and evidence.","C.1: if a Vickrey-price expression is intended, provide a source-supported formula or a precise binding for 'last second qualified bidder' and 'last bid'; otherwise confirm that no formal expression is available and keep the constraints not_formalized."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
